#!/usr/bin/env python3

"""About:
sway-quit uses readline to get input

Usage:
main commainds:
  reconfigure, quit, sway

sway commands:
  reload, edit config, select terminal (mod+Enter), select Menu (mod+D)

quit commands:
  reboot, exit sway, shut down, kill (select and kill process)

reconfigure <variable>:
  reconfigure allows you to reconfigure variables used in sway-quit

  You can:
  Set which editor should open sway config.
  Select path to sway config.
  change commands which should reboot, shut down, etc. your computor (note different OS may have different commands).
  chage where sway-quit's config should be located.

Example:
> sway-quit reconfigure quit reboot
loginctl reboot
# written into ~/.local/share/anom-bins/sway-quit.config
# confstyle=ini
[quit]
reboot = "loginctl reboot"
"""
